{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## How this was found, and the one thing NOT proven\n\nFound while verifying whether Gerrit change 2673 had landed. `git merge-base --is-ancestor\n459e1d1b099f origin/main` returned NO, but the change HAD merged — as `9e6a0e436520`, found by\n`Change-Id`. That prompted a sweep of `is-ancestor` uses across the repo, of which this script\nwas the only site where the rewritten sha changes an operator-visible answer.\n\n**Not proven:** I did not establish WHY `feature/s1-windows-sweep-probe` was rebased on submit\nwhile the other four branches were not. The rebase-on-submit explanation fits (`main` is\nRebase-If-Necessary; the branch is exactly 1 commit ahead of main with its Change-Id present\nunder a different sha), but I did not rule out the alternative — an amended patchset never\nsubmitted in that exact form, with an equivalent commit landing separately. Settle that before\nwriting the fix: it decides whether Change-Id lookup alone suffices, or whether patch-id\nequivalence is also needed.\n\n## Store-health context from the same pass\n\n`rebar doctor`: exit 0, 0 stale locks, all six lock legs free, all three MCP client configs ok.\nIts 17 findings are all pre-existing `mis-escalated` link records (blocking-link promotion\nrecording an endpoint that differs from the resolved comparable pair) — unrelated to this bug\nand not new.\n\n## Two observations for the \"checks that don't check\" sweep\n\n1. The CREATE of this ticket returned `push_status: {state: pending, reason:\n   push-transport-failed, detail: \"git timed out after 30s\", unpushed: 3}` — three ticket commits\n   not yet shared to `origin/tickets` — and `rebar doctor` did not surface that condition in the\n   output I read. FLAGGED AS UNVERIFIED, not as a finding: I read only the tail of doctor's\n   output, so a sync section may exist above it. If it does not, \"store reports healthy while\n   writes are invisible to every other session\" is the same failure shape as this bug.\n\n2. The MCP server degraded during this same pass: two `comment_ticket` calls exceeded 120s and\n   were backgrounded, and one then FAILED outright after 300s with \"sent no response or progress\".\n   Tracker writes were completed via the local CLI instead. Recorded here because it is live\n   evidence for `witted-invisible-roan` (MCP endpoint 502s during long gate jobs) and because a\n   silently-dropped MCP write is itself a check-that-does-not-check: the caller's write appears\n   issued and simply never lands."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788638111347742001,"uuid":"51fef1f3-3cbe-451f-93bb-30aab2ed7a82"}